\subsection{Atmospheric Module Convergence (DMR Mesh)}

The atmospheric module solves the Navier--Stokes and heat transport equations on
a dynamically refined spherical mesh (DMR) spanning thermosphere, troposphere,
and stratosphere. High-gradient boundary turbulence was maintained without
floating-point underflow, and convergence exhibited stable harmonic dampening
across all spatial layers.

\subsection{Dataset Encryption Pipeline Verification}

Raw FITS observational data were ingested through an AES-256 secure layer into
encrypted storage clusters supporting homomorphic processing within SGX/SEV
secure enclaves. No plaintext leakage was observed. Cryptographic integrity
checks passed, with FIPS 140-3 compliance verified across all handshakes.

\subsection{Stress Test Verdict}

All subsystems maintained operational integrity under peak stress conditions.
ASAOP is theoretically validated for continuous high-load operation in
multi-domain astrophysical and atmospheric simulations with secure data
processing.